3. Java  start()  versus  run() 

C++ has no separate  start()  method.

void task() {
    std::cout << std::this_thread::get_id() << '\n';
}

int main() {
    task();                 // Runs in current thread
    std::thread t(task);    // Starts a new thread immediately
    t.join();
}

A completed  std::thread  cannot be restarted. Construct another thread object instead.

