12. Reader-writer lock

Use  std::shared_mutex :

#include <mutex>
#include <shared_mutex>

class SharedValue {
    int value_ = 0;
    mutable std::shared_mutex mutex_;

public:
    int read() const {
        std::shared_lock lock(mutex_);
        return value_;
    }

    void write(int value) {
        std::unique_lock lock(mutex_);
        value_ = value;
    }
};

•  std::shared_lock : multiple readers may hold it.
•  std::unique_lock : one exclusive writer.
• Fairness and writer preference are implementation-dependent.

