15. Executors and thread pools

The C++20/23 standard library has no direct equivalent of Java's  ExecutorService ,  ScheduledExecutorService , or  ThreadPoolExecutor .

Common options are:

• Boost.Asio  thread_pool 
• oneTBB
• Folly
• A custom queue + worker threads
• C++26 execution facilities, where supported

Example using Boost.Asio:

#include <boost/asio/post.hpp>
#include <boost/asio/thread_pool.hpp>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    boost::asio::thread_pool pool(4);

    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
        boost::asio::post(pool, [i] {
            std::cout << "Task " << i << '\n';
        });
    }

    pool.join();
}

Approximate mappings:

┌─────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Java executor operation │ Typical C++ implementation                               │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ execute(task)           │ Queue a void callable                                    │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ submit(task)            │ Queue a std::packaged_task, return its future            │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ shutdown()              │ Stop accepting work, drain queue, join workers           │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ shutdownNow()           │ Request cooperative cancellation and discard queued work │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ invokeAll()             │ Submit multiple tasks, call get() on every future        │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Fixed pool              │ Fixed collection of worker threads                       │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Cached pool             │ Dynamically sized custom/library pool                    │
├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Scheduled executor      │ Timer/event-loop library such as Boost.Asio              │
└─────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

C++ cannot safely kill running worker threads. Immediate shutdown must use cooperative cancellation.

