19. CompletableFuture equivalent

Standard  std::future  does not support:

•  thenApply 
•  thenCombine 
•  exceptionally 
•  allOf 
•  anyOf 
• Continuation callbacks

There is therefore no direct standard C++20 equivalent to  CompletableFuture .

Libraries providing composable asynchronous operations include:

• Boost.Asio
• Folly Futures
• Qt  QFuture 
• HPX futures
• oneTBB flow graph
• C++20 coroutines with an asynchronous runtime

A basic chain can be approximated with another async task:

auto first = std::async(std::launch::async, [] {
    return std::string("Hello");
});

auto second = std::async(
    std::launch::async,
    [future = std::move(first)]() mutable {
        return future.get() + " World";
    }
);

std::cout << second.get() << '\n';

This works, but the second task blocks a thread while waiting. A proper continuation-aware runtime avoids that inefficiency.

