20. Most important C++ differences

1. Prefer  std::jthread  over  std::thread  for automatic joining and cancellation support.
2. C++  volatile  is not a synchronization mechanism; use  std::atomic .
3. An exception escaping a thread calls  std::terminate() .
4. Concurrent unsynchronized container access causes undefined behavior rather than a reliable exception.
5. Standard C++20 has futures but no  CompletableFuture -style continuations.
6. Standard C++20 has no general executor or thread-pool API.
7. Use RAII lock wrappers instead of manually calling  lock()  and  unlock() .
8. Cancellation is cooperative; never forcibly terminate threads.
